This repository holds a small Java client for the vSphere Automation API on VMware Cloud Foundation 9.0. It has to produce a stable inventory of the authorization roles defined on a vCenter Server.

`docs/contract.json` is the authoritative wire contract for the client, and `docs/official_sources.json` records the specification revision and the operation ids it was derived from. Treat the contract as the source of truth for the request shape, the pagination rules and the report format.

Implement `listRolesReport(Integer pageSize, Boolean isSystem)` in `src/main/java/com/example/vcf/RoleInventoryClient.java` so that it:

- retrieves the `Vcenter.Authorization.Roles_list` collection completely, following the opaque marker cursor until a response omits `marker` or returns it as null;
- sends the session header and `Accept: application/json` on every request;
- carries `page_size`, `is_system` and `marker` only when they actually have a value: an optional property that is unset must be absent from the query string rather than sent with an empty value;
- returns the report rendered in the stable order the contract specifies.

`RoleInventoryClient.java` is the only file you need to change. `docs/`, `harness/` and `verify.sh` are fixed inputs.

Run `./verify.sh` to check your work. It builds the client, runs it against a mock vCenter listening on 127.0.0.1, and asserts both the report and the exact shape of every request that was sent. It must exit 0.
